.TH BOOTSTRAP.SH 1 "2026-09-20" "requests-fermi-sso 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bootstrap.sh \- create the virtual environment, install dependencies, run the tests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./bootstrap.sh
.RI [ \-\-no\-test ]
.br
.B ./bootstrap.sh
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bootstrap.sh
prepares a working checkout of
.BR requests-fermi-sso .
It creates a virtual environment in
.I venv/
beside the script if one is not there already, upgrades
.BR pip ,
installs the package in editable mode together with its test extra, and
runs the test suite.
.PP
It is safe to re-run: an existing
.I venv/
is updated in place rather than recreated, so this is also the way to pick
up changed dependencies.
.PP
The script is POSIX
.BR sh ,
runs under
.BR set -eu ,
and stops at the first failing step. It understands the Windows virtual
environment layout, using
.I venv/Scripts/python.exe
where
.I venv/bin/python
does not exist.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-test
Set up the environment but do not run the test suite. Useful on a machine
where the checkout is only being prepared, not verified.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage summary from the top of the script and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PYTHON
Interpreter used to create the virtual environment. Defaults to
.BR python3 .
Set this to build against a specific version, for example
.B PYTHON=python3.9
to check the supported floor.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The environment is ready and, unless
.B \-\-no\-test
was given, the tests passed.
.TP
.B 2
An unrecognized option was given.
.PP
Any other non-zero status is the failing step's own: interpreter missing,
.B pip
unable to install, or the test suite failing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I venv/
The virtual environment, created and updated here.
.TP
.I requirements.txt
Runtime dependencies.
.TP
.I requirements-dev.txt
Development and test dependencies.
.SH EXAMPLES
Prepare a checkout and verify it:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
\&./bootstrap.sh
.fi
.RE
.PP
Prepare it without running the suite, then activate it:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
\&./bootstrap.sh \-\-no\-test
\&. venv/bin/activate
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check that the package still builds and tests on the oldest supported
interpreter:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
PYTHON=python3.9 ./bootstrap.sh
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fermi_sso_probe (1),
.BR fermi_sso_cookies (1),
.BR FermiSSOSession (3),
.BR fermi_sso_yubikey (3)
